WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
SOC 2 is an auditing and attestation framework developed by the American Institute of

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.160
Certified Public Accountants,

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.565
commonly known as the AICPA.

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:11.895
It is used to evaluate whether an organization has designed and operates controls that

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:14.480
support one or more Trust Services Criteria.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.160
Those criteria relate to security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.400
and privacy.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.360
In everyday language,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.070
SOC 2 helps customers understand whether a service provider has practices in place to

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:25.915
protect systems,

00:00:25.915 --> 00:00:29.680
information, and commitments that matter to the customer relationship.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.740
SOC 2 is especially common for technology companies, SaaS providers, cloud services,

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.270
managed service providers,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.300
and other organizations that handle customer data or operate important systems on behalf

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:39.904
of others.

00:00:39.904 --> 00:00:42.840
A key point is that SOC 2 is not a certification.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.210
It is an independent attestation performed by qualified auditors.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.500
The resulting report describes the audit scope, the criteria included,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.690
the controls evaluated, testing performed, and the auditor's opinion.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.300
Customers use SOC 2 reports during vendor reviews, procurement, risk assessments,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.000
renewals, and security questionnaires.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.925
The report gives them a structured way to understand how the organization approaches trust

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:04.360
and operational control.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:09.020
For employees, SOC 2 matters because the report is based on real operating practices.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.920
Policies, access controls, change records, monitoring activities, training,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.120
incident response, and evidence all come from normal work across the organization.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.085
This course provides an educational overview of SOC 2.

00:01:20.085 --> 00:01:24.720
It is not professional legal, accounting, regulatory, assurance, or compliance guidance.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.220
The goal is to help you understand the concepts and your role in supporting trustworthy

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:28.955
operations.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:33.520
The most useful way to think about SOC 2 is as a trust conversation supported by evidence.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.680
The report helps an organization explain what it does, how controls are evaluated,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.640
and why customers can place confidence in the services being provided.
